        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present No. 57 Hampton Wood Avenue, a superb two-bedroom, two-bathroom apartment ideally positioned within this highly sought-after residential development in Dublin 11.\n\nSituated on the first floor, this spacious apartment offers well-proportioned accommodation throughout and is ideally suited to first-time buyers, downsizers and investors alike. The property comprises a welcoming entrance hallway which leads into a bright and spacious open-plan kitchen and living area, creating an excellent space for both everyday living and entertaining. The living room benefits from direct access to a private balcony, providing a fantastic outdoor space.\n\nThere are two generous double bedrooms, both benefiting from built-in wardrobes. The main bedroom further benefits from a private ensuite, while a separate family bathroom is conveniently located off the hallway.\n\nExternally, residents benefit from a designated car parking space located in the basement. Further features include gas-fired central heating, double-glazed windows throughout and a BER rating of B. Management fees are approximately 2400 per annum.\n\nHampton Wood Avenue enjoys an excellent and highly convenient location with a wealth of amenities and transport links right on its doorstep. There is numerous Dublin Bus stops immediately beside Hampton Wood, providing regular services to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas, while Dublin Airport is also easily accessible by public transport and is approximately 15 minutes by car. Finglas Village, Charlestown Shopping Centre, Clearwater Shopping Centre and IKEA are all within easy reach, alongside a fantastic selection of local shops, cafés, restaurants, supermarkets, schools, sports clubs and recreational facilities. The area also benefits from close proximity to Tolka Valley Park, Johnstown Park and the National Botanic Gardens. The nearby Luas Red Line at Broombridge provides an additional excellent transport option, with further connectivity planned as part of the proposed Luas Finglas extension. The M50 Motorway is just minutes away, providing easy access to Dublin Port, Dublin Airport and all major national routes, while the N2, N3 and M50 road networks are all within convenient reach.\n\nContact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 0861985247 or 015411455 to arrange a viewing or register your interest.\n\nAdditional Features\n• C. 64 sqm\n• BER B\n• Superb two-bedroom, two-bathroom apartment\n• Built 2007\n• Lift access\n• Situated on the first floor\n• Two generous double bedrooms\n• Built-in wardrobes in both bedrooms\n• Ensuite off main bedroom\n• Family bathroom\n• Bright open-plan kitchen and living room\n• Private balcony accessed from living room\n• Useful storage room off hallway\n• Gas-fired central heating\n• Double glazing throughout\n• Designated basement car parking space\n• Management fees approx. 2400 per annum\n• Excellent residential development\n• Excellent public transport links\n• Easy access to Dublin City Centre\n• Close to Finglas Village, Charlestown Shopping Centre, Clearwater Shopping Centre and IKEA\n• Minutes from the M50 Motorway\n• Approximately 15 minutes from Dublin Airport\n• Ideal for first-time buyers, downsizers and investors"
      },
